  "_commit": {
    "id": "2fec690b923848868bd64d2809817731fa4ad98d",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "fix: quote sql_fun() IN-list values via dbQuoteString (0.99.27)\n\nsql_fun,DuckDBTable-method built its return_type/function_type IN (...)\npredicates by pasting user-supplied strings between hardcoded quotes with\nno escaping, so a return_type containing a ' (e.g. \"x') OR 1=1 --\") broke\nout of the SQL literal before hitting dbGetQuery(). function_type wasn't\nactually exploitable (match.arg() constrains it to a fixed enum first),\nbut both now go through DBI::dbQuoteString(conn, ...), the same\nconnection object already used elsewhere in the method.\n",
    "time": 1789225886
  },
